  },
  "114": {
    "codebook_rule": [
      "1",
      "2"
    ],
    "document_id": "114",
    "explanation": "The release states that Democrats and Republicans \"passed legislation\" and presents Senate Majority Leader Harry Reid as urging the President to sign the bill. It treats the bill as a legislative accomplishment associated with Reid and the Senate Democrats, even while urging final presidential action. It also describes a provision included in \"our legislation,\" implying legislative success in including that provision. Therefore it qualifies as credit-claiming under rules concerning legislative accomplishments and concrete outcomes.",
