  },
  "2955": {
    "codebook_rule": ["1", "4"],
    "document_id": "2955",
    "explanation": "Senator Domenici announces a defense contract awarded to Honeywell in New Mexico and presents himself as pleased with the outcome, mentioning his membership on the Senate Defense Appropriations Subcommittee. The text strongly implies the senator helped secure or announce a concrete benefit for his state, satisfying rule 1 and rule 4. There is some ambiguity because it does not explicitly say he secured the contract, but the framing as an announcement by the senator of a state benefit tied to his appropriations role supports credit-claiming.",
    "label": "1"
  },
  "3335": {
    "codebook_rule": ["1", "4"],
    "document_id": "3335",
    "explanation": "The release announces that Holocaust-era archives will be opened and states that Senator Biden long advocated for opening them, wrote to ambassadors urging ratification, pressured remaining countries, and wrote an op-ed. It presents the completed ratification/opening as a concrete outcome connected to his advocacy, satisfying rules 1 and 4. It does not describe an award or legislative enactment, so rules 3 and 5 are not used.",
